   <h2>Architecture</h2>
-  <p>The patch changes the core connection and ApiProxy policy rather than adding exceptions to individual API routes. The browser receives an explicit server authority marker, and the settings layer chooses host-backed state from that marker even when the page is not loopback.</p>
+  <p>The patch changes the core connection and ApiProxy policy rather than adding exceptions to individual API routes. The browser receives an explicit server authority marker, and the settings layer chooses host-backed state from that marker even when the page is not loopback. Agent defaults point at the pi-ai multi-provider route for the same model family, and in-process subagents inherit the parent session's live model route instead of a stale creation-time provider.</p>
   <h2>Source and reproducibility</h2>
-  <p>The installer pins the official upstream commit recorded in <code>UPSTREAM-COMMIT.txt</code> and applies <code>patches/open-authority-web-only.patch</code>. The active base composition does not mount the DeepSeek provider; its source package remains available for intentional overlays.</p>
+  <p>The installer pins the official upstream commit recorded in <code>UPSTREAM-COMMIT.txt</code> and applies <code>patches/open-authority-web-only.patch</code>. The active base composition does not mount the official DeepSeek adapter; its source package remains available for intentional overlays, and the default model selection uses the pi-ai <code>deepseek</code> route.</p>
